{"id":58343,"ord":29,"n_segments":204,"prev":58342,"next":58344,"doc":{"id":"68359","title":"68359_Zutty Singleton oral history interview","collection":"rutgers","inst":"Rutgers — Institute of Jazz Studies","interviewee":"Zutty Singleton","interviewer":"","date":"","year":"","source_url":"https://rucore.libraries.rutgers.edu/rutgers-lib/68359/","url":"https://thisismattmiller.github.io/linked-jazz-2026-transcripts/?t=68359"},"chapter":"New Orleans bands, Louis and the Lyric","title":"Baby Dodds and Red Happy's drum contest","category":"person_portrait","summary":"Zutty knew Baby Dodds in New Orleans; Dodds and Red Happy had a drumming contest on Zutty's drums, and a Preservation Hall drummer says he learned from Red Happy.","period":"1910s","year_from":1910,"year_to":1919,"words":115,"start":[42,0],"end":[43,0],"url":"https://thisismattmiller.github.io/linked-jazz-2026-transcripts/?t=68359#s58343","tags":{"places":[{"name":"New Orleans","focus":0,"type":"city"}],"venues":[{"name":"Preservation Hall","focus":0,"city":"New Orleans"}],"bands":[{"name":"Preservation Hall Jazz Band","focus":0,"leader":null}]},"people":[{"name":"Red Happy","qid":null,"n":2},{"name":"Louis Armstrong","qid":"Q1779","n":1},{"name":"Baby Dodds","qid":"Q374629","n":1},{"name":"Buster Bailey","qid":"Q362522","n":1},{"name":"C.I.","qid":null,"n":1}],"story":{"theme":14,"theme_name":"Drummers and drumming: who played what, and how","community":42,"community_name":"Great drummers: who they admired and why","core":true},"blocks":[{"p":42,"b":0,"s":"MR. DANCE","x":"Of course Buster knew of him really, really knew, Buster knew all about Louis by that time."},{"p":42,"b":1,"s":"MR. SINGLETON","x":"Oh yes."},{"p":42,"b":2,"s":"MR. DANCE","x":"You mentioned Baby Dodds and I mean I take it you knew him in New Orleans?"},{"p":42,"b":3,"s":"MR. SINGLETON","x":"Why sure, sure. Him and (Red Happy?) had a contest on my drums."},{"p":42,"b":4,"s":"MR. DANCE","x":"Who did?"},{"p":42,"b":5,"s":"MR. SINGLETON","x":"Red Happy."},{"p":42,"b":6,"s":"MR. DANCE","x":"Red Happy? Where's he from?"},{"p":42,"b":7,"s":"MR. SINGLETON","x":"He's from New Orleans. A real hell of a drummer too."},{"p":42,"b":8,"s":"MR. DANCE","x":"Red Happy."},{"p":42,"b":9,"s":"MR. SINGLETON","x":"Red Happy."},{"p":42,"b":10,"s":"MR. DANCE","x":"Never heard of him before."},{"p":42,"b":11,"s":"MR. SINGLETON","x":"Happy ( ?)."},{"p":42,"b":12,"s":"MRS. SINGLETON","x":"(Yeah, ALL THE OLD NEW ORLEANS people talk about him ?)."},{"p":42,"b":13,"s":"MR. DANCE","x":"Yes?"},{"p":42,"b":14,"s":"MR. SINGLETON","x":"That's what this boy that drums with Preservation Hall band."},{"p":42,"b":15,"s":"MR. DANCE","x":"Yes. Cie?"},{"p":42,"b":16,"s":"MR. SINGLETON","x":"(C.I.?). He said that's how"},{"p":43,"b":0,"s":"MR. SINGLETON","x":"he learned how to play drums."}]}